# project.done

Completed: 2026-09-15 (THE FINAL BLITZ lane, commits 3b6ca9a..HEAD of the
blitz range; releases v3.43.0, v3.44.0, v3.45.0 on PyPI, plus cquarry
v1.22.0 shipped upstream under cross-repo grant #117).

## What shipped

- 3.43.0, the record-integrity batch: the phase-1 manifest filename is
  unique per batch (the final audit's HIGH), provenance seeds `Z-Lib`
  (the renamed enum value), bindery's gate-accepted EPUB repairs mirror
  into the sealed lossy records, the Calibre-running refusal is
  lock-class exit 1 everywhere, `--export` propagates its refusals,
  the TUI scope-typo notice survives the terminal reset, and
  `--restrict ... --tags` obeys the universe (with the audit's L2.2
  ratings-key claim recorded as a misdiagnosis and the correct key
  pinned by a test).
- cquarry 1.22.0 (upstream, #117): `CalibreDB.precedent_tags()` (the
  promoted 4-table JOIN) plus the publish-path hardening; CalibreQuarry
  3.44.0 consumed it and bumped the floor.
- 3.44.0, the truth-and-hardening batch: the frontend's last
  unrecorded raw-SQL reads retired, the seven lying headers/comments
  truthed, the publish path SHA-pinned and least-privileged (with a
  tag-protection ruleset and actions-only dependabot), the spec floor
  collapsed to floor-plus-bumps, the README test section says 559
  tests/27 files (from 373), and the version-sync test now guards the
  spec header, the spec floor, and the roadmap stamp.
- 3.45.0, the gated features + cleanup: `--rename-entity`,
  `--set-author-sort`, `--set-title-sort`, the `--trash` listing and
  `run trash --empty|--expire` lifecycle, the live em-dash layer
  eliminated, every comment LOW and polish LOW executed, scripts exec
  bits normalized, and PEP 639 license metadata.
- Eight gates asked and answered (all Recommended options taken);
  Brandon's push grant is standing for this lane; the Release cutoff is
  recorded as intentional (Releases exist v3.37.0+); the dead dev
  dependency group is deleted; REPORT-12-Sept.md moved to docs/; the
  stale venvs and the retired .claude/settings.local.json are removed
  locally.

## Reopen conditions (the recorded future work)

- Roadmap box "New work noticed in the final blitz": the dest-list
  constants module, the `_backup_db` triplication, the per-mode
  `--format` corners, bindery's unmirrored `manual_watermark_repair`
  decisions, the lossy double-manifest wrinkle, and the UI-only pypi
  tag policy (Settings > Environments > pypi > Deployment branches and
  tags > allow `v*.*.*`; REST policies reject tag deployments).
- The audit-block residuals: the release-cutoff is decided (recorded),
  the feature backlog (L4 ranks 5-11: find_duplicate_books swap,
  `--health --format json`, tag-tree rollups, `run fts-index`,
  addition_timeline year granularity, identifierless advisory, TUI set
  writes) remains roadmap-boxed, and the TUI screenshot TODO needs a
  live curses capture (Brandon's hands or a driven terminal).
- cquarry's own final-audit block (landed there 2026-09-15) is
  cquarry's lane; its no-force-push ruleset on main is the piece its
  box still names.
